## 1. Introduction to Cryptography

### Why We Need Cryptography
Cryptography is used to protect three core properties:

| Property | Description |
|---|---|
| **Confidentiality** | Ensures only intended parties can read the data |
| **Integrity** | Ensures data has not been altered in transit |
| **Authenticity** | Confirms the identity of who sent the data |

### Real-World Examples
- Logging into a website — credentials are encrypted before being sent to the server
- SSH sessions — client and server establish an encrypted tunnel so no one can eavesdrop
- Online banking — your browser verifies the server's certificate to confirm you're talking to the real bank and not an attacker

> A standard for handling payment card data securely is known as **PCI DSS** (Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard).

### Key Terms

| Term | Description |
|---|---|
| **Plaintext** | Original readable data before encryption |
| **Ciphertext** | Encrypted data that cannot be read without a key |
| **Encryption** | Converting plaintext → ciphertext using a key |
| **Decryption** | Converting ciphertext → plaintext using a key |

