## 12. Recognizing Password Hashes

Different hashing algorithms produce hashes with recognizable patterns. Understanding these helps identify which algorithm was used.

| Hash Format | Algorithm |
|---|---|
| `$1$...` | MD5-crypt |
| `$2y$...` / `$2b$...` | bcrypt |
| `$6$...` | SHA-512-crypt |
| `$y$...` | yescrypt |
| 32 hex characters | MD5 |
| 40 hex characters | SHA-1 |
| 64 hex characters | SHA-256 |

> Automated tools like **hash-identifier** can help, but learning to recognize hashes manually is an important skill.

